# Website Viewer (cavekit-flash.md R7), the corpus's form: it draws, and without its own site's data
# (humbird0.com) its ActionScript runs away once it is tapped. That is the task it can do here: the player asks
# "Kill this Action Script?" through the card's dialog, the finger answers, the dialog goes and the card still
# shows the movie's page. A limit of the title, not of the browser: the same file needs its site anywhere.
id: flash-app-form
section: Flash
item: A Flash app does its task, the form whose script runs away without its site: the player's "Kill this Action Script?" dialog comes, the finger answers it and the page stays
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8097/title/website-viewer
kit: cavekit-flash.md R7
wait rect m 40
wait still m 25
expect flash-drawn m yes
stage-tap m 640 480 320 240
expect dialog present 30
shoot asked
chrome dialog-ok
expect dialog answered 8
wait still m 10
expect flash-drawn m yes
expect url website-viewer
